--
-- Test Description
-- This test checks the operation of the TX exposed FIFO interface (read).
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- * Checks the operation of the tx_r_mod signal
-- * Checks the operation of the tx_r_data_rdy signal
-- * Checks combinations of the tx_r_sop and other control signals
-- * Checks the operation of the tx_r_control signal
-- * Checks the operation of the handshaking signals
-- * Checks the operation of the tx_r_status signal
-- * Checks the operation of the tx_r_flushed signal
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--
--  tx_r_mod testing
--  ----------------
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts and then enable 
--     transmit in 100M half duplex mode from a 128-bit FIFO data bus.
--  3. Transmit a frame of 16 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
--  4. Transmit a frame of 17 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
--  5. Transmit a frame of 18 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
--  6. Transmit a frame of 19 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
--  7. Transmit a frame of 20 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
--  8. Transmit a frame of 21 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
--  9. Transmit a frame of 22 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
-- 10. Transmit a frame of 23 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
-- 11. Transmit a frame of 24 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
-- 12. Transmit a frame of 25 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
-- 13. Transmit a frame of 26 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
-- 14. Transmit a frame of 27 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
-- 15. Transmit a frame of 28 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
-- 16. Transmit a frame of 29 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
-- 17. Transmit a frame of 30 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
-- 18. Transmit a frame of 31 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
-- 19. Transmit a frame of 32 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
-- 20. Check statistics for above operations.
--
--  tx_r_data_rdy testing (also includes combinations of control signals)
--  ---------------------
-- 21. Transmit a 64 byte frame. After the TX MAC has performed the SOP read
--     drop the tx_r_data_rdy signal. Queue up another 16 byte frame, but
--     tx_r_data_rdy is only asserted once an apb trigger is performed. By 
--     delaying this trigger until after the first frame has completed, verify
--     that the TX MAC does not perform any more FIFO reads after it has 
--     seen the EOP for the first frame. Then verify that the 2nd frame is 
--     successfully transmitted once tx_r_data_rdy is asserted.
-- 22. Transmit a 64 byte frame. Ensure that tx_r_data_rdy is high at the EOP
--     read of the first frame. This means that the TX MAC will keep reading
--     the FIFO searching for the next SOP.
--     On each successive read provide combinations of the control and data
--     signals except SOP. Ensure that these combinations are ignored.
--     Finally provide an SOP and a valid 16 bytes frame. Ensure that this
--     frame is correctly transmitted.
-- 23. Force a start of packet read by asserting tx_r_data_rdy, but before the
--     tx_r_valid is signalled for the read, drop tx_r_data_rdy.
--     This should be ignored and the frame will be transmitted successfully.
-- 24. Check statistics for above operations.
--
--  tx_r_control testing
--  --------------------
-- 25. Transmit a frame of 32 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     On the first FIFO read set the tx_no_crc bit, and on the second FIFO read
--     ensure that the tx_no_crc bit is low. Verify that the frame is
--     transmitted without padding and CRC and the the correct number of bytes
--     are transmitted and correct status is reported.
-- 26. Transmit a frame of 32 bytes with padding and CRC.
--     On the first FIFO read reset the tx_no_crc bit, and on the second FIFO
--     read ensure that the tx_no_crc bit is high. Verify that the frame is
--     transmitted with padding and CRC and the the correct number of bytes
--     are transmitted and correct status is reported.
-- 27. Check statistics for above operations.
--
--  handshaking, tx_r_status and tx_r_flushed testing
--  -------------------------------------------------
-- 28. These signals are checked in the following tests:
--       handshaking : All FIFO tests
--       tx_r_status : [0] too_many_retries  - col_retry_16_1gm_fifo
--                     [1] late_coll_occured - col_64_1gm
--                     [2] collision_occured - col_64_1gm
--                     [3] tx_r_underflow    - tx_und_err_fifo
--       tx_r_flushed: col_retry_16_1gm_fifo, col_64_1gm, tx_und_err_fifo
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------



--******************************************************************************
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--******************************************************************************
wait_states 3
bus_grant_delay 3



--******************************************************************************
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts and then enable 
--     transmit in 100M half duplex mode from a 128-bit FIFO data bus.
--******************************************************************************
apbwr(60)  4c 00000001  -- enable soft config fifo port bit when available
apbrd      4c 00000001  -- check enable soft config bit when available

apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbrd      30 00000000  -- check that all interrupts are now enabled
apbwr      04 00680000  -- enable 100M mode into 128-bit bus
apbwr      00 00000008  -- enable transmit
apbrd      14 00000000  -- check tx status, wait for tx_go when enabled
apbrd      14 00000008  -- check tx status, always tx_go when enabled



--******************************************************************************
--  3. Transmit a frame of 16 bytes with no padding or CRC.
--     The correct tx_r_mod value must be used on the final read. Verify
--     that the correct number of bytes are transmitted and correct status is
--     reported.
--******************************************************************************

apbrdf     14 00000008  "Scenario 1: Check tx_r_mod - 16 bytes frame"
                        -- check tx status, always tx_go in fifo mode
                        -- and trigger data ready for first test

-- Supply data to TX FIFO interface
--
-- CONTROL =  <RESERVED>, NO CRC, FLUSH, UNDERFLOW, RDY, ERR, SOP, EOP.
--
--              CONTROL   MOD  STATUS          DATA
fifo_rd(apb)    01001010   0   00000000    8877665544332211
fifo_rd         01001001   0   00000000    10ffeeddccbbaa99

-- check for correct preamble, SFD, data, pad and crc
txd   55555555555555d511223344
txd   5566778899aabbccddeeff10


-- check status on reception of transmit complete interrupt
apbrd(int) 24 00000080  "Scenario 1: Complete"
                        -- check interrupt status - transmit complete
apbrd      14 00000028  -- tx status - frame transmitted, always enabled
apbwr      14 00000028  -- clear it



